/home/runner/work/_temp/shurik-runtime-47mmoz/source/ARCHITECTURE.md:52:The iteration action inherits native provider environment variables and cloud configuration. Pi AI resolves authentication; Shurik supplies no per-request API-key override, interactive login flow, or persistent credential store. The existing `opencode-api-key` input remains an optional environment alias. Credentials never become action configuration, worker-request JSON, or saved control fields. Publication redaction includes provider key/token variables and cloud credentials present in the environment. Bundled metadata comes from the installed Pi AI package; unlisted IDs use provisional metadata. Additional custom endpoints need an adapter integration.
/home/runner/work/_temp/shurik-runtime-47mmoz/source/ARCHITECTURE.md:58:The action fetches engine source into a temporary checkout outside the task checkout. Builds use the engine's package lock. Consumer code is cloned separately from the consumer's source/work branch. At initialization, workflow definitions come from the default branch even when `source_ref` selects older task source, because the Actions token cannot introduce other workflow versions on new branches. Consumer repositories do not need Shurik source, a package.json, or any Shurik dependencies. Model, prompt, checkpoint interval, and ignored task snapshot selections come from the consumer, not the engine checkout.
/home/runner/work/_temp/shurik-runtime-47mmoz/source/ARCHITECTURE.md:78:The built-in GitHub token has contents/PR/Actions write permissions for the consumer worker job. Start and control check the dispatch actor's repository write permission. Secrets stay in Actions inputs/environment and do not enter command-line arguments. Fork contributor CI remains read-only and receives no model key.
/home/runner/work/_temp/shurik-runtime-47mmoz/source/ARCHITECTURE.md:80:`create-pr` is an optional action/CLI setting; the workflow adapter calls it `create_pr`. The default `auto` attempts a draft PR when task changes exist. Successful creation records `createPr: true`; GitHub's specific repository-setting denial records `createPr: false` and continues. Explicit `false` skips PR API calls, while `true` enables an attempt. Other API errors retain the normal failure/recovery behavior. The durable control field is carried across iterations and can be changed on resume; `auto` retries permission discovery after repository settings change. Permission discovery uses the normal PR request and does not require an administration token.
